{"id": "EUVD-2026-59179", "enisaUuid": "479075d3-f8b2-314f-b379-07d4e4b5c92b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: arm64: nv: Drop bogus WARN for write to ZCR_EL2\n\nIt is entirely possible for a guest to write to the ZCR_EL2 sysreg alias\nwhile in a nested context, as it is expected if FEAT_NV2 is advertised\nto the L1 hypervisor.\n\nGet rid of the bogus WARN which, since the hyp vectors were installed at\nthis point, has the effect of a hyp_panic...", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:55:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:14", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6561597dba97e3e8479a9919bda172cf43eb902c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5000bcae71c869cba6674c326fec2d8ad659ae3a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7deadbc5dab5b8e2316364603bc6281129c8461c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9f1667098c6ae7ec81a9a56859cfdacb822aa0d0"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pjc6-4q26-frjf", "CVE-2026-72280"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1f862330-e74e-3332-97ea-c3f69101fd19", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "2456078b-00b6-3cdd-ba43-c7f33ab7db5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3b67220d-ecd0-3ccd-9832-f7b5faecea8a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0cfc85b8f5cf3b77463d61542191c75ba0cc3a5f <5000bcae71c869cba6674c326fec2d8ad659ae3a"}, {"id": "3d0c5d65-0879-362b-bf95-585e58a3a67c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0cfc85b8f5cf3b77463d61542191c75ba0cc3a5f <7deadbc5dab5b8e2316364603bc6281129c8461c"}, {"id": "4b2dbaae-ba2d-3fd6-8858-6bd3eaa68022", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "5ddd19d9-c